# Drafted by Gemini (R24 hovel), edited.

~ door
Narrator: A slanted hovel leans in the quiet glade, its mossy boards weathered grey while hundreds of stick-and-bone idols click softly in the pine boughs overhead.
* Go in -> go_in
* Look at the idols first -> idols
* Leave it -> END

~ go_in
Narrator: You put your hand to the warped planks and step over the threshold into the musty dark.
move ct_hovel
-> END

~ idols
Narrator: Twigs bound with sinew and bleached knuckles hang from the needles, knocking together like dry teeth in a draft you cannot feel.
* [Perception DC 13] Look closely at the idols -> idols_lore | idols_lore_f
* Take one down -> idols_take
* Leave them be -> END

~ idols_lore
Narrator: Look long enough and the crooked twigs take the shape of things you left behind in life: a sagging porch, a faithful hound, a face you loved.
-> idols

~ idols_lore_f
Narrator: Try as you might to find a pattern in the knots, they remain nothing more than dead wood and old marrow.
-> idols

~ idols_take
Narrator: {name} reaches up into the cold needles and closes a hand around the nearest cord.
check Charisma DC 18 -> idols_ok | idols_hex

~ idols_ok
Narrator: The cord parts without a sound, and the little bundle comes down cold and quiet into your palm.
-> idols

~ idols_hex
Narrator: The clicking stops all at once across the glade, and every little face of bone and twig turns slowly toward {name}.
set ct_idols_hex
disadvantage checks 2h: the idols' hex
-> idols

~ arrive
Narrator: Behind you, the heavy door swings shut on its own, and the iron latch drops home with a dull, final clack.
set ct_hovel_entered
-> END

~ paintings
Narrator: Six chipped paintings run round the leaning walls, their faded pigments peeling above a bent table and a broken chair.
* [Nature DC 13] Read the paintings -> paintings_lore | paintings_f
* [Insight DC 13] Read the faces in the paintings -> paintings_lore | paintings_f
* Search the room instead -> paintings_skip
* Leave -> END

~ paintings_lore
Narrator: You trace the six panels in the hush: a young queen in a green wood, a gift freely given, a bitter betrayal, a long grief, a dark bargain, and a consuming fire.
Narrator: Sitting a while with that old sorrow lets you catch your breath and bind your scrapes before the road ahead.
time +60
heal 2d8 party
-> fire_starts

~ paintings_f
Narrator: Damp and age have flaked too much away, leaving only the sixth and final panel clear: a wall of hungry red flame.
-> paintings

~ paintings_skip
Narrator: You turn your back on the peeling walls and leave the old queen's story to the dust.
-> paintings

~ fire_starts
set ct_paintings_read
set ct_hovel_fire
Narrator: The painted flames on the sixth wall begin to blister and hiss, and thick black smoke curls out from the boards as the room remembers how it burned.
-> END

~ bed
Narrator: In the corner sits a rotting bedstead, its straw tick split and smelling of wet leaves and mice.
* [Investigation DC 13] Search under the bed -> bed_ok | bed_f
* Leave it -> END

~ bed_ok
Narrator: Half buried in the mouldering straw beneath the frame, {name} hooks a rusted tin of dried pigments and stiff-bristled brushes.
give painters_supplies
set ct_painter_found
-> bed

~ bed_f
Narrator: {name} sweeps an arm through the dark under the frame and comes back with nothing but grey dust and a dry beetle husk.
-> bed

~ escape
Narrator: Smoke chokes the low rafters and flames lick up the walls, while the heavy door holds fast against its self-dropped latch.
* [Sleight of Hand DC 20] Pick the lock -> out | burn
* [Athletics DC 25] Force the door -> out | burn
* [Athletics DC 15] Smash through a slatted window -> out | burn
* Hold your breath and wait -> burn

~ burn
Narrator: The heat presses in like an oven door, searing your lungs and blistering your skin as the dry timber roars.
damage 1d10 fire party
-> escape

~ out
Narrator: You spill out coughing onto the cold pine needles, and the moment the last boot clears the sill, the fire inside dies to cold ash.
set ct_hovel_escaped
set ct_hovel_done
move ct_wytchwood:from_hovel
-> END
